Task: Extract a pure financial-year helper (Phase 1, Tier 1)
Track: fy_tax_pack_20260729

SUMMARY
New pure module lib/tax/fy.ts, covered by tests/lib/tax/fy.test.ts.
Exports: fyBounds, currentFyEndYear, mostRecentCompletedFyEndYear,
formatFyLabel, selectableFyEndYears, plus AU_FY_START_MONTH/DAY.

FILES
- lib/tax/fy.ts (new)
- tests/lib/tax/fy.test.ts (new) - 20 tests

WHY
Two defects motivated extracting this rather than patching in place:

1. Timezone drift. The tax-report page builds FY bounds with the
   local-time Date constructor then calls toISOString(). At UTC+10,
   new Date(2025, 6, 1).toISOString() is "2025-06-30" - the FY start is
   a day early, so one day of the prior year's expenses leaks in. The
   helper works entirely in UTC.

2. Wrong default year. The page infers the FY from new Date(), which
   yields the IN-PROGRESS year. On 29 July 2026 that is 2026-27, not the
   2025-26 year a 2026 return covers. mostRecentCompletedFyEndYear
   returns the year that has actually finished, and treats a year as
   incomplete until the day after it ends.

Month-end arithmetic derives the end date as "day before next year
starts" rather than assuming a month length, so leap years are correct.
A 1 January start is handled as a single calendar year.

VERIFICATION PERFORMED
- Red phase: CI=true npm test failed with "Cannot find package
  '@/lib/tax/fy'" before implementation, confirming the tests exercise
